# Jira commit linking

Every **task-related** commit must include a work-item key so Jira's **Development** panel (commits / branches / PRs) links correctly when GitHub is connected. See [Atlassian Smart Commits](https://support.atlassian.com/jira-software-cloud/docs/process-issues-with-smart-commits/) — we use **issue keys only**, not smart-command syntax.

## Required subject format

```
<type>(<scope>)[<ISSUE-KEY>]: <imperative summary>
```

| Part | Rule |
|------|------|
| `<type>` | Conventional Commits: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf` |
| `<scope>` | Same allowed scopes as `01-git-workflow.mdc` (`web`, `backend`, `worker`, …) |
| `[<ISSUE-KEY>]` | **Mandatory** on task commits — square brackets, uppercase project key |
| Summary | Imperative mood; whole subject ≤72 chars |

### Issue key precedence

1. **Jira leaf issue** — `[DO-N]` when the task exists on board (orchestrator JIRA SYNC, user named `DO-*`, or roadmap row has a Jira mirror via `Roadmap ID`)
2. **Roadmap only** — `[P2-01]` when no Jira issue exists yet
3. **Combined batch** — primary leaf key in brackets; list siblings in session memory (e.g. `[DO-24]` for shared-file batch touching DO-24/25/26)

### Examples

```bash
# GOOD — Jira work
feat(web)[DO-129]: add Playwright auth fixture
fix(worker)[DO-128]: skip expiry while vehicles en route

# Session memory is gitignored — do NOT use chore(memory)[DO-N] commits.
# Verifiers post Done/FAIL summaries to Jira (orchestrator jira-board.md).

# GOOD — roadmap-only (no Jira mirror)
feat(auth)[P2-01]: add register endpoint with bcrypt cost 12

# GOOD — verifier / plan (key matches task)
chore(plan)[DO-133]: mark P8-07 verified

# BAD — key at end (old format)
feat(web): add auth fixture (DO-129)

# BAD — missing key on task work
feat(web): add auth fixture

# BAD — smart commit commands (MCP owns Jira sync)
feat(web)[DO-129]: add fixture #time 2h #comment done
```

## Smart Commits — do NOT use in commit messages

Jira sync (status, worklog, comments) is handled by **MCP** in orchestrated runs (`addWorklogToJiraIssue`, `transitionJiraIssue`, `addCommentToJiraIssue`). Never put these in commit subjects or bodies:

- `#time`, `#comment`, `#resolve`, `#close`, or any `#<transition>` command

Issue keys alone link commits to work items; smart commands would **duplicate** worklogs and can transition issues at the wrong time.

## Exceptions (no issue key required)

- Pure repo hygiene with **no** task ID: `chore(repo): bump turbo to 2.x` (rare; prefer a DO issue when in doubt)
- Merge commits from integration: `chore(repo)[DO-47]: integrate orchestrator batch`

## Enforcement

- **Execution agents:** both session-memory and implementation commits include `[DO-N]` or `[P*-*]`
- **Verifiers:** Layer 3 — FAIL if a task commit subject lacks a valid issue key when Jira sync was in scope
- **Orchestrator prompts:** pass leaf `DO-N` in GIT block; see `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/prompt-templates.md`
